---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import PageHeader from '../components/ui/PageHeader.astro';
import { site } from '../config/site';
---

<BaseLayout pageType="privacy" title="Privacy | Sean Carney" description="How seancarneymusic.com collects and uses information, and your California privacy choices.">
  <PageHeader title="Privacy" intro="Plain language. Last updated November 2026." />
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container prose body">
      <h2>What we collect</h2>
      <p>When you send an inquiry, we receive the details you provide (name, email, phone, event details), how you found the site, such as the referring website or campaign, and, if you choose to tell us, how you heard about Sean and the name of whoever referred you (so Sean can thank them). We use this only to respond to you and to understand which channels and referrals bring inquiries. So no inquiry is lost if our booking system is briefly unavailable, a copy is held with our web host (Cloudflare) for 90 days and then deleted automatically. If an inquiry has not yet reached our booking system by then, its copy is kept until it does, for at most 180 days.</p>
      <h2>Analytics</h2>
      <p>If you use the music quiz, your song favorites and Do Not Play choices are saved only in this browser tab. They are sent to SCE only when you choose to share them and submit an inquiry. Closing the tab or using the clear-data control removes those saved choices.</p>
      <p>We use privacy-friendly analytics that do not use advertising cookies, plus session analytics that mask form inputs. These help us understand which pages are useful and where the site can be clearer.</p>
      <p>Your browser keeps a small visit record for this site: the date of your first visit, when you last visited and how many visits. It holds no name, email or identifier. We use it to tell new from returning visitors, to mark what is new since your last visit, and to send an anonymous weekly count (for example "a visitor first seen in week 45 came back") that contains nothing that identifies you.</p>
      <h2>Advertising</h2>
      <p>If advertising pixels are enabled, they load only when your browser does not send a Global Privacy Control signal and you have not opted out below.</p>
      <p>Under the same conditions (you allowed cookies, have not opted out and send no Global Privacy Control signal), when you send an inquiry our server also tells Meta that the conversion happened, so ad results are measured accurately. That message contains your email and phone only in hashed form, which Meta uses to match it to its own records, plus your browser's IP address and user agent. Nothing is sent when any of those conditions is not met.</p>
      <h2 id="scout">Scout, the AI assistant</h2>
      <p>Scout is an automated AI assistant, not Sean or a member of his team. It can check whether a date looks open, suggest formats for your day, show wedding films, answer questions about Sean's performances, and send an inquiry when you ask it to.</p>
      <p>When AI replies are on, your messages and the page you are on are sent to our AI provider (Anthropic) to generate replies. The conversation is kept only in your browser tab and is cleared when you close the tab or choose "Clear chat". We do not store chat transcripts on our servers.</p>
      <p>To improve the site we keep anonymous counts of the topics people ask about and the event dates they check. Unrecognized questions may be kept for up to 120 days with email addresses, phone numbers and street addresses removed. None of this is linked to you.</p>
      <p>Scout can prepare an inquiry from what you typed, but nothing is sent until you check the details and press Send. Then those details (such as your name, email and event) go to Sean's booking system, exactly as with the inquiry form. Scout never signs you up for text messages; that consent is only collected on the inquiry form.</p>
      <p>Scout can make mistakes. Availability shown in chat is indicative, and every booking is confirmed by Sean personally.</p>
      <h2>Text messages</h2>
      <p>If you opt in to text messages on the inquiry form, messages relate to your inquiry. Message frequency varies; message and data rates may apply. Reply STOP to opt out at any time. Mobile numbers and SMS consent are never sold or shared with third parties for marketing. Full program terms: <a href="/terms#sms">Terms</a>.</p>
      <h2 id="choices">Your privacy choices</h2>
      <p>California residents may opt out of the sale or sharing of personal information. Use the switch below, or send a Global Privacy Control signal from your browser, which we honor automatically.</p>
      <label class="toggle"><input type="checkbox" data-optout /> Do not sell or share my personal information</label>
      <label class="toggle"><input type="checkbox" data-analytics-consent /> Allow optional analytics cookies</label>
      <p class="status" data-optout-status aria-live="polite"></p>
      <p><button type="button" class="btn btn--ghost" data-clear-site-data>Clear data saved in this browser</button></p>
      <p class="status">Removes your consent choice, A/B test assignment, visit attribution, visit record, Scout conversation and any saved inquiry draft from this browser. Data you already sent to Sean is handled through the contact below.</p>
      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>Questions or deletion requests: <a href={`mailto:${site.email.management}`}>{site.email.management}</a>.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<script>
  import { clearSiteData } from '../lib/storage';
  import { adTrackingAllowed, setAdOptOut } from '../lib/analytics/privacy';
  import { track } from '../lib/analytics/track';
  import { onPage } from '../lib/lifecycle';

  onPage(() => {
    const box = document.querySelector<HTMLInputElement>('[data-optout]')!;
    const status = document.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-optout-status]')!;
    const gpc = (navigator as Navigator & { globalPrivacyControl?: boolean }).globalPrivacyControl;
    box.checked = !adTrackingAllowed();
    if (gpc) {
      box.disabled = true;
      status.textContent = 'Your browser is sending Global Privacy Control, so you are already opted out.';
    }
    const ac = document.querySelector<HTMLInputElement>('[data-analytics-consent]')!;
    try { ac.checked = localStorage.getItem('sc_consent') === 'granted'; } catch { /* noop */ }
    ac.addEventListener('change', () => {
      (window as Window & { __scSetConsent?: (v: string) => void }).__scSetConsent?.(ac.checked ? 'granted' : 'denied');
      status.textContent = ac.checked ? 'Analytics cookies allowed.' : 'Analytics cookies off.';
    });
    document.querySelector('[data-clear-site-data]')?.addEventListener('click', () => {
      const n = clearSiteData();
      ac.checked = false;
      box.checked = false;
      status.textContent = n ? 'Cleared. This browser no longer holds any data from this site.' : 'Nothing was stored in this browser.';
    });
    box.addEventListener('change', () => {
      setAdOptOut(box.checked);
      status.textContent = box.checked ? 'Opted out. Advertising pixels will not load.' : 'Preference cleared.';
      track('privacy_optout', { opted_out: box.checked });
    });
  }, '[data-optout]');
</script>

<style>
  .body h2 { font-size: var(--step-2); margin: 2.5rem 0 0.75rem; color: var(--text); }
  .body h2:first-child { margin-top: 0; }
  .toggle { display: flex; gap: 0.75rem; align-items: center; margin-top: 1rem; color: var(--text); cursor: pointer; min-height: 44px; }
  .toggle input { width: 20px; height: 20px; accent-color: var(--accent); }
  .status { margin-top: 0.5rem; font-size: var(--step--1); }
</style>
